      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Churg-Strauss syndrome is an uncommon multisystem disease involving small and medium-sized arteries, capillaries, veins, and venules. It is characterised by the presence of asthma, hypereosinophilia, and evidence of vasculitis affecting a number of organs. It is important for acute medical physicians to recognise this condition as delayed diagnosis results in a higher morbidity and mortality. Here we describe a case of Churg-Strauss syndrome in a 41 year old woman presenting with a recurrent painful rash. The clinical manifestations and management of this condition are discussed."},
